original:
To extend this pattern to more complex cases, simply pass additional sets as positional arguments.
```python
a = {5, 10}
b = {15, 20}
c = {25, 30}
d = {35, 40}
combined = set().union(a, b, c, d)
print(combined)  # Output: {5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40}
```

variant:
To extend this pattern to more intricate cases, simply pass further sets as positional arguments.
```python
a = {5, 10}
b = {15, 20}
c = {25, 30}
d = {35, 40}
combined = set().union(a, b, c, d)
print(combined)  # Output: {5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40}
```
